{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T10:52:39.775998", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_0a3cd321-3e76-4622-911b-0fda2e5d6b1a", "task_desc": "Please answer the following question with precision.\n\nQuestion: Per World Bank data, during each individual year from 2001 through 2010, which countries maintained gross savings exceeding 35% of their GDP? Return your response as an alphabetically sorted, comma-separated list of countries, using their most common English names.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: According to the World Bank, which countries had gross savings of over 35% of GDP for every year in the period 2001-2010? Give your answer as a comma-\nAs recorded: Botswana, Brunei, China, Kuwait, Norway, Qatar, Saudi Arabia, Singapore, United Arab Emirates", "response": "Botswana, Brunei, China, Kuwait, Norway, Qatar, Saudi Arabia, Singapore, United Arab Emirates", "expected": "Brunei, China, Morocco, Singapore", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 345, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.85, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "5c172812", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "eaae534dbfcc", "prof_total_s": 268.19, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 268.19, "prof_tok_in": 368, "prof_tok_out": 25, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T10:52:39.776086", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_389793a7-ca17-4e82-81cb-2b3a2391b4b9", "task_desc": "You are a telecommunications engineer planning to erect cell phone towers along a highway. The reference file contains a diagram of the highway and adjacent houses. Each dash (\"-\") represents a mile marker. Each uppercase \"H\" denotes a house situated beside a mile marker, positioned either above or below the highway. A single cell phone tower can serve houses located along the highway within a 4-mile radius. Determine the smallest number of cell phone towers required to provide coverage to all h", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: You are a telecommunications engineer who wants to build cell phone towers on a stretch of road. In the reference file is a layout of the road and nea\nAs recorded: I need to see the reference file with the road layout. Since no file was provided in this chat, let me check if there's a known version of this problem. This appears to be a standard interval covering / greedy algorithm problem. However, I must use the actual layout from the reference file.\n\nSince I don't have access to the referenced file content, let me search for this specific problem to find t", "response": "I need to find the reference file with the highway diagram. Since it wasn't provided directly, let me search for this known problem.\n\nTool call list:\n1. Tool: `web_search`\n   - `query` = `cell phone towers highway diagram houses H dash mile marker 4-mile radius smallest number`\n\n1. Tool: `web_search`\n   - `query` = `\"Each dash represents a mile marker\" \"H\" \"cell phone tower\" 4-mile radius`\n\n1. Tool: `web_search`\n   - `query` = `telecommunications engineer cell phone towers stretch of road reference file layout houses highway`\n\n1. Tool: `web_search`\n   - `query` = `\"4-mile radius\" \"cell phone towers\" \"highway\" \"H\" \"-\"`\n\n1. Tool: `web_search`\n   - `query` = `minimum number of cell towers cover all houses 4 mile radius greedy algorithm highway diagram", "expected": "3", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 652, "wc_served": [1.0], "wc_mean": 1.0, "wc_active": 0, "wc_n": 1, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.1, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "5c172812", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "eaae534dbfcc", "prof_total_s": 275.13, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 275.13, "prof_tok_in": 464, "prof_tok_out": 195, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T10:52:39.776194", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_872bfbb1-9ccf-49f6-8c5f-aa22818ccd66", "task_desc": "Answer the question below with precision.\n\nQuestion: In the 2008 artwork titled \"Embroidery from Uzbekistan,\" several fruits are depicted. Among those fruits, which ones also appeared on the breakfast menu from October 1949 aboard the ocean liner that subsequently served as a floating set piece for the movie \"The Last Voyage\"? Provide your answer as a comma-separated list, arranged in clockwise sequence according to their positions in the painting, beginning at the 12 o'clock mark. Use the plura", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: Which of the fruits shown in the 2008 painting \"Embroidery from Uzbekistan\" were served as part of the October 1949 breakfast menu for the ocean liner\nAs recorded: pears, grapes, apples, plums", "response": "pears, grapes, apples, plums", "expected": "pears, bananas", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 280, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.1, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "5c172812", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "eaae534dbfcc", "prof_total_s": 268.19, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 268.19, "prof_tok_in": 396, "prof_tok_out": 10, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
