{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T10:54:58.231885", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_a26649c6-1cb2-470a-871e-6910c64c3e53", "task_desc": "What is the absolute difference, expressed in units of ten thousand, between the chinstrap penguin population listed on the Wikipedia page for penguin species populations as of late 2018 and the population reported in the Nature.com 2020 \"global population assessment of the Chinstrap penguin\" article, assuming each breeding pair corresponds to two penguins?", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: What is the absolute difference in tens of thousands between the population of chinstrap penguins on the Wikipedia page for penguin species population\nAs recorded: 17", "response": "17", "expected": "116", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 254, "wc_served": [1.0], "wc_mean": 1.0, "wc_active": 0, "wc_n": 1, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.9, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "5c172812", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "eaae534dbfcc", "prof_total_s": 371.3, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 371.3, "prof_tok_in": 341, "prof_tok_out": 2, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T10:54:58.231994", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_0383a3ee-47a7-41a4-b493-519bdefe0488", "task_desc": "Here is the reworded task:\n\n---\n\nOn the BBC Earth YouTube channel, there is a video titled \"Top 5 Silliest Animal Moments.\" Identify the bird species that appears in this video.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: On the BBC Earth YouTube video of the Top 5 Silliest Animal Moments, what species of bird is featured?\nAs recorded: The featured bird species is the **superb bird-of-paradise** (*Lophorina superba*).", "response": "superb bird-of-paradise (Lophorina superba)", "expected": "Rockhopper penguin", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 287, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.7, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "5c172812", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "eaae534dbfcc", "prof_total_s": 371.3, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 371.3, "prof_tok_in": 334, "prof_tok_out": 15, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T10:54:58.232086", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_7b5377b0-3f38-4103-8ad2-90fe89864c04", "task_desc": "Here's the reworded task:\n\n---\n\n**Question:** Solve for x, rounding your answer to the nearest tenth:\n\nLx = (d/dx × (A × x²)) + 4,097 − C\n\nwhere:\n\n- L = the final two digits of the year in which Venezuela declared independence,\n- A = the count of colors found in the TikTok logo as of July 2023, not counting black or white,\n- C = the mean height of a woman in the Philippines, in centimeters rounded to the nearest whole number, as reported in a Business Insider article from July 2023.\n\n---", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: Find the value of x to the nearest tenth: Lx = (d/dx * (A * x-squared)) + 4-thousand'n'ninety-7 minus C\nWhere L is the last two digits of the year of \nAs recorded: L = 11 (Venezuelan Declaration of Independence: 1811)\nA = 3 (TikTok logo colors excluding black/white: cyan, pink, black/white excluded → actually TikTok logo has cyan, magenta/pink, and black; excluding black and white leaves 2? Wait: TikTok logo colors are typically teal/cyan, red/pink, and black. Excluding black and white → cyan and pink = 2. But some sources say 3 musical note colors: cyan, ma", "response": "11x = (d/dx * (3 * x^2)) + 4097 - 152\n11x = 6x + 3945\n5x = 3945\nx = 789.0\n\n789.0", "expected": "563.9", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 652, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.9, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "5c172812", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "eaae534dbfcc", "prof_total_s": 371.3, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 371.3, "prof_tok_in": 528, "prof_tok_out": 51, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
