{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T11:06:40.350507", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_3627a8be-a77f-41bb-b807-7e1bd4c0ebdf", "task_desc": "Answer the question below with precision.\n\nQuestion: The British Museum holds an artifact cataloged under museum number 2012,5015.17 — it is the shell of a specific mollusk species. Based on the abstract of a 2021 Science Advances research paper, beads crafted from the shells of this very species were discovered to be at least how many thousands of years old?", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: The object in the British Museum's collection with a museum number of 2012,5015.17 is the shell of a particular mollusk species. According to the abst\nAs recorded: The object 2012,5015.17 in the British Museum is a shell of the mollusk species *Laevistrombus tubulatus* (formerly *Strombus* sp.). A Science Advances 2021 article abstract states that beads made from *Laevistrombus tubulatus* shells found in East Timor are at least 42 thousand years old.\n\n42", "response": "42", "expected": "142", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 546, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.9, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "5c172812", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "eaae534dbfcc", "prof_total_s": 664.65, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 664.65, "prof_tok_in": 436, "prof_tok_out": 2, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
