{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T11:24:02.129149", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_11af4e1a-5f45-467d-9aeb-46f4bb0bf034", "task_desc": "Please answer the following question with precision.\n\nQuestion: Compared to the encoder described in the \"Attention is All You Need\" paper, how many additional blocks (also referred to as layers) does the BERT base encoder possess?", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v2]\nTask: Compared to the encoder from the architecture introduced in \"Attention is All You Need,\" h\nAs recorded: 6\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: How many more blocks (also denoted as layers) in BERT base encoder than the encoder from t\nAs recorded: BERT base encoder has 12 blocks (layers). The encoder in \"Attention is All You Need\" (the base Transformer) has 6 layers. 12 - 6 = 6.\n\n6\n\nVersion lineage (later supersedes earlier):\n  v1 -> v2: score -100%", "response": "6", "expected": "6", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 545, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "5c172812", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "eaae534dbfcc", "prof_total_s": 1051.41, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 1051.41, "prof_tok_in": 406, "prof_tok_out": 2, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
